@node CMacs Journal Daily
@chapter CMacs Journal Daily: The Day's Note

@cindex journal daily note
@cindex daily note
@cindex weekly note
@cindex what I worked on today

@code{cmacs-journal-daily} writes ``what I worked on today'' as an Org
note in your PARA notes tree, from the activity journal (@pxref{CMacs
Journal}).  The note has two parts, and only one of them needs a model.

@lisp
(cmacs-journal-mode 1)          ; the journal: what had the focus
@end lisp

Then @kbd{M-x cmacs-journal-daily}.  The note is
@file{~/Documents/notes/02_areas/dailies/@var{YYYY-MM-DD}.org}.

Five things about it, stated plainly:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{The facts need no model.}  Time per project, application and
site, a timeline, the longest stretches, files, pages and finished
agent runs are computed in Elisp from the journal's spans.  The totals
are the ones @code{cmacs-journal-report} shows, because both call
@code{cmacs-journal-summarize}.
@item
@strong{A summary is optional, off by default, and local by default.}
With @code{cmacs-journal-daily-summary} a model adds a few sentences
written from those facts.  The default provider is ollama.  A provider
that is not local is refused unless
@code{cmacs-journal-daily-allow-remote} says otherwise, and then it
asks first.
@item
@strong{Today's privacy rules apply to old spans.}  A span was filtered
when it was recorded.  It is filtered again, under the rules as they
are now, before a single total is computed---so a title recorded last
week, before you wrote the rule that hides it, is in neither the note
nor the prompt.
@item
@strong{The file is yours.}  A daily you wrote by hand is never
reordered or overwritten.  One subtree, marked with the property
@code{CMACS_JOURNAL_DAILY}, belongs to this feature and is replaced in
place.  Nothing else in the file is touched.
@item
@strong{It is human-only.}  There is no brigade tool, no MCP tool and
no D-Bus method, and the commands refuse to run for an agent or a
remote caller.
@end itemize

It is part of the journal: built with @option{--with-cmacs-journal},
pure Elisp.  The summary needs @option{--with-cmacs-ai}; everything
else does not.

